    {
     "heading": "What happened",
     "text": "Tasia Fortune, a 29-year-old mother, was found hanging from a tree in Mississippi in August. Police confirmed her death was a homicide and stated that the hanging was staged after she died. Three suspects have been arrested. Officers believe the killing arose from a drug dispute. Her mother expressed shock, as the exact cause of death remains undisclosed."
    },
    {
     "heading": "Why it matters",
     "text": "The discovery caused fear in the majority-black city of Jackson due to the state's history of lynchings and racial violence. The case left the local community on edge and led lawmakers to demand federal investigations."
